# Security-review gate, per docs/10-cross-cutting/testing.md §release-gates.
#
# Changes under these paths need a security-focused review in addition to the
# normal one. GitHub enforces this only when the named team exists and branch
# protection requires review from code owners — the file alone is advisory, so
# the rule is written here and the enforcement is a repo setting.
#
# The list is the spec's, mapped onto real paths:
#   sunrise-crypto · sunrise-sync · sunrise-server::auth ·
#   sunrise-storage::migrations · pairing/onboarding paths in sunrise-core

/crates/sunrise-crypto/                  @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-crypto-test-vectors/     @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-sync/                    @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-server/src/auth/         @justin13888
# Was `src/ws.rs`, until ADR-0023 deleted it. `api/sync.rs` is what took over
# the session's credential handling: token expiry, the mid-session refresh, and
# the device re-check that ends a stream a revoked device is already holding.
/crates/sunrise-server/src/api/sync.rs   @justin13888
# `api/signed.rs` is the single device-signature verification path: the four
# extractors every typed route is built from, and the only place a request
# becomes a verified (Principal, Device) pair. `sunrise-http-sig` is the
# canonicalisation and signature primitive underneath it, shared with the relay
# client — so a change to either is a change to the binding itself, and the
# `auth/` rule above does not reach either one.
/crates/sunrise-server/src/api/signed.rs @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-http-sig/                @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-storage/migrations/      @justin13888

# Pairing and onboarding: the key-distribution path. `keychain.rs` holds the
# vault root and `vault_lock.rs` guards single-writer access, so both belong
# under the same gate as the pairing crate itself.
/crates/sunrise-pairing/                 @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-onboarding/              @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-core/src/keychain.rs     @justin13888
/crates/sunrise-core/src/vault_lock.rs   @justin13888

# The gates themselves. A change that weakens a check should be as visible as a
# change to the thing it checks — the determinism and redaction gates were both
# silently unenforceable until this session.
/.github/workflows/                      @justin13888
/.github/scripts/                        @justin13888
/clippy.toml                             @justin13888
/deny.toml                               @justin13888
